# Cold Chain Monitor (small demo)

A small, rules-based app that checks whether temperature-sensitive shipments stayed
within their product limits. It shows three decisions: **Compliant**, **Non-compliant**,
and **Review required** (insufficient or uncertain evidence). It never marks a shipment
compliant just because no violation was found.

All data is synthetic and generated locally from a fixed seed.

## Project layout

```
backend/
  main.py       FastAPI app: JSON API under /api, serves the frontend
  database.py   SQLAlchemy models, schema setup, dataset loading
  logic.py      Rules engine, demo data generator, ground-truth evaluation
frontend/
  index.html    Page shell and navigation
  style.css     Styling
  app.js        Pages, API calls, temperature chart (inline SVG)
```

## Run it

```bash
cd backend
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate          # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install fastapi uvicorn sqlalchemy
uvicorn main:app --reload
```

Open http://127.0.0.1:8000

The server creates `backend/cold_chain.db` (SQLite) and generates 50 shipments on
startup. Each start resets the demo data to the same seed, so results are repeatable.

To use MySQL 8 instead, install `pymysql` and set:

```bash
export DATABASE_URL="mysql+pymysql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:3306/cold_chain"
```

## Pages

- **Dashboard**: KPIs, status distribution, shipments needing attention, temperature trend.
- **Shipments**: search by ID, filter by status, paginated table.
- **Shipment detail**: policy, readings chart, decision reasons, custody timeline,
  excursions, and missing-data intervals.
- **Evaluation**: precision, recall, F1, and false-compliant rate against ground truth.
- **Data & Export**: regenerate demo data with a chosen size and seed; download CSV or JSON.

## API

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/health` | Health check |
| GET | `/api/summary` | Dashboard KPIs and attention list |
| GET | `/api/shipments?q=&status=&page=&size=` | Paginated, filtered list |
| GET | `/api/shipments/{code}` | Full detail with readings, decision, custody |
| GET | `/api/export/csv` or `/api/export/json` | Shipment decisions export |
| GET | `/api/evaluation` | Comparison with ground truth |
| POST | `/api/data/generate?count=50&seed=20261022` | Replace demo data |

Interactive docs: http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs

## Rules

- **Limits**: a temperature exactly at a limit is in range. Only values strictly outside are out of range.
- **Duration**: from the first out-of-range reading to the first in-range reading after it, using real timestamps.
- **No bridging**: an out-of-range run is split at any gap longer than the allowed maximum.
- **Confirmed vs. uncertain**: an excursion is confirmed only if some reading is beyond the logger's accuracy tolerance. Otherwise it is uncertain.
- **Decision order**:
  1. `NON_COMPLIANT`: a confirmed excursion is longer than the allowed duration.
  2. `REVIEW_REQUIRED`: a missing-data gap, an uncertain reading, or a custody problem (missing PICKUP or DELIVERY, or events out of order).
  3. `COMPLIANT`: none of the above.
- **Isolation**: each shipment is evaluated only on its own readings and custody events.

## Limitations

- SQLite by default. MySQL is supported through `DATABASE_URL` but is not the default in this demo.
- No login. The regenerate endpoint is open, so this is for local demo use only.
- Only one threshold policy per product and no version history.
- No separate exception-resolution workflow or audit trail.
- The ground-truth scenarios were written alongside the rules, so the 100% evaluation
  score shows the rules are consistent with the scenarios, not that they are accurate on real shipments.
- The charts are hand-drawn SVG, not Recharts, to keep the frontend to three plain files.